> diff x^3 - 3x
d/dx x^3 - 3x = 3x^2 - 3
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> diff x^4 + x^2*y + y^3 x y
∂²/∂y∂x x^4 + x^2*y + y^3 = 2x
  holds wherever the formula is defined
  check: each order matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 3e-13)
> F'' x^4
_(F'': real, x: real) = F''*x^4
  -> real
> limit sin(x)/x x -> 0
limit of sin(x)/x as x -> 0:
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(1) = lim cos(x)
  = 1 (from both sides)
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1
    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1
    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees
> limit 1/x x -> 0+
limit of 1/x as x -> 0+ (from the right):
  1/x -> inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0+)
  = inf
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 10, 160, 2560, 40960, 655360, 20971520
    the values grow without bound (+): agrees
> limit 1/x x -> 0-
limit of 1/x as x -> 0- (from the left):
  1/x -> -inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0-)
  = -inf
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): -10, -160, -2560, -40960, -655360, -20971520
    the values grow without bound (-): agrees
> limit (x^2-1)/(x-1) x -> 1
limit of (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1) as x -> 1:
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (2x)/(1) = lim 2x
  = 2 (from both sides)
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 1.9, 1.99375, 1.999609375, 1.999975586, 1.999998474, 1.999999952
    extrapolated (Richardson): 2 (estimated error 0): agrees
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 2.1, 2.00625, 2.000390625, 2.000024414, 2.000001526, 2.000000048
    extrapolated (Richardson): 2 (estimated error 7e-17): agrees
> limit x - sqrt(x^2+1) x -> inf
limit of x - sqrt(x^2 + 1) as x -> inf:
  inf - inf: times the conjugate: (x)^2 - (sqrt(x^2 + 1))^2 over their sum = -1/(x + sqrt(x^2 + 1))
  = 0
  numeric (x = 10*2^k, k = 0..21): -0.04987562112, -0.003124969483, -0.0001953124925, -1.220703125e-05, -7.629394645e-07, -2.384149411e-08
    extrapolated (Richardson): 9.6299625269e-17 (estimated error 1e-16): agrees
> limit sin(1/x) x -> 0
limit of sin(1/x) as x -> 0:
  1/x -> inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0+)
  1/x -> inf: sin(1/x) keeps oscillating between -1 and 1
  = none (it oscillates between -1 and 1)
  the limit does not exist
